This directory contains a benchmark that aims to determine the ability of Geneva's
optimization algorithms to get close to the global optimum of a given target function.
It uses the GFunctionIndividual for its tests.

The measurement is the quality reached, and the time taken, as a function of the
problem's dimension: the same function is optimized at 2, 4, 8, ... 512 parameters,
ten times per dimension, and the mean and spread of both quantities are plotted.

For those numbers to be comparable across dimensions every row must get the same
budget, so this directory's config-overrides.json fixes the run at 1000 iterations
and switches the stall criterion off. Do not "fix" that back to the library
defaults: with a stall halt in place each dimension stops wherever it happens to
plateau, and the curve then measures the stall criterion as much as the problem.
The dimension list itself is the benchmark's own default, in
GOptimizationBenchmarkConfig.hpp, where the next rungs (1024 and up) sit commented
out for a deliberate, longer study.
